From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 23:27:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(setup): wire Graphiti memory MCP server into Claude and
 Cursor configs

When memory.backend resolves to graphiti (deps > FORGE_MEMORY_BACKEND >
.forge/config.yaml) and the config passes the same strict validity check
forge doctor uses (assertMemoryConfigValid), forge setup now appends the
graphiti-memory descriptor from lib/memory/graphiti-mcp.js to the MCP
render for BOTH .mcp.json (Claude) and .cursor/mcp.json (Cursor).

- Local backend (default) stays byte-identical to the Context7-only render
- Invalid/incomplete graphiti config: one-line notice, skip, never crash
- Renderer untouched; read->merge->write still preserves user servers
- docs/guides/memory-backends.md updated: wiring is delivered, not a
  fast-follow (Codex config.toml remains manual)

Kernel issue: 40f21e91-45f2-4eb3-9b47-b4cd3080fedd
ROADMAP: Memory that finds things

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
